<div class="callout">
  <b>&#9432; About this audit</b>
  This report is the result of a full static analysis of the MCM Cloud CX prototype codebase. All findings are based on reading the source files: <code>src/mcm/scripts.ts</code> (1.2 MB, 14 JS engine modules), <code>src/mcm/markup.ts</code>, <code>src/mcm/mcm.css</code>, and <code>src/routes/index.tsx</code>. Items are classified by severity: Critical, High, Medium, and Low.
</div>

<hr>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
     ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<h2>1. Executive Summary</h2>

<table class="summary">
  <tr>
    <td><span class="sum-num c-red">11</span><span class="sum-label">Broken or<br>Non-functional Elements</span></td>
    <td><span class="sum-num c-amber">5</span><span class="sum-label">UX Dead-Ends &amp;<br>Navigation Gaps</span></td>
    <td><span class="sum-num c-blue">15</span><span class="sum-label">UX Improvement<br>Suggestions</span></td>
    <td><span class="sum-num c-green">8</span><span class="sum-label">Quick Wins<br>(Low-effort, High-impact)</span></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>
  MCM Cloud CX is an impressive and deeply functional contact-centre simulation. The majority of the platform — queues, flows, telephony, WFM, agent workspace, performance dashboards — works as designed. However, a set of high-visibility buttons and features are either silently broken or only partially implemented, which erodes user trust. This report identifies those gaps and offers prioritised, actionable fixes.
</p>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 2: BROKEN ELEMENTS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>2. Broken &amp; Non-Functional Elements</h2>

<div class="callout">
  <b>&#9888; Architecture note</b>
  All interactivity is implemented as vanilla JavaScript injected via <code>dangerouslySetInnerHTML</code>. Buttons without an <code>onclick</code> attribute are silently inert — no browser error is thrown, users simply see no response when they click.
</div>

<h3>2A — Buttons &amp; Icons with No Handler (completely silent)</h3>

<table class="issues">
  <tr>
    <th style="width:26%">Element</th>
    <th style="width:18%">Location</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Expected Behaviour / Fix</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">"Audit Viewer" button<br><span style="font-weight:normal;color:#5b6a7d;font-size:9.5pt;">Secondary button in Admin index header</span></td>
    <td>Admin → Home</td>
    <td class="sev-critical">CRITICAL</td>
    <td>Should open the Audit Log drawer. Add <code>onclick="auditDrawer()"</code> — the function exists in Engine v13.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">"What's New" button<br><span style="font-weight:normal;color:#5b6a7d;font-size:9.5pt;">Primary button in Admin index header</span></td>
    <td>Admin → Home</td>
    <td class="sev-critical">CRITICAL</td>
    <td>Should open the What's New dropdown. Add <code>onclick="dd('wnddm')"</code> — both the handler and dropdown HTML already exist.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Directory people card icons<br><span style="font-weight:normal;color:#5b6a7d;font-size:9.5pt;">Phone / Email / Chat / Edit icons on contact cards</span></td>
    <td>Directory → People cards</td>
    <td class="sev-critical">CRITICAL</td>
    <td>Completely inert &lt;div&gt; elements with no onclick. Phone should trigger a call, email should open compose, chat should open a session, pencil should open the person editor.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">"Export" secondary button<br><span style="font-weight:normal;color:#5b6a7d;font-size:9.5pt;">Present on ~40 admin pages</span></td>
    <td>All admin pages</td>
    <td class="sev-high">HIGH</td>
    <td>No onclick on any instance. Should call page-specific CSV export or <code>mcmExport()</code>. Currently misleads users into thinking export works.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">⊙ What's New icon (top bar)</td>
    <td>Top navigation bar</td>
    <td class="sev-medium">MEDIUM</td>
    <td>Renders as a character glyph with no handler. Should open <code>dd('wnddm')</code>.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">? Help icon (top bar)</td>
    <td>Top navigation bar</td>
    <td class="sev-medium">MEDIUM</td>
    <td>No onclick. Should open <code>dd('helpddm')</code> — the dropdown exists.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>2B — Placeholder Buttons (show a toast instead of working)</h3>

<table class="issues">
  <tr>
    <th style="width:26%">Element</th>
    <th style="width:18%">Location</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Current Behaviour &amp; Recommended Fix</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Script Editor → "Preview"</td>
    <td>Contact Center → Script Editor</td>
    <td class="sev-high">HIGH</td>
    <td>Shows toast: <i>"Preview opened in agent view (demo)"</i>. Should render the script in the agent workspace sidebar so trainers can test it.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Architect → "Debug"</td>
    <td>Routing → Architect Flow Editor</td>
    <td class="sev-high">HIGH</td>
    <td>Shows toast: <i>"Debug session started"</i>. Should launch the existing Test Call flow walk-through, not just a toast.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Architect → "Save"</td>
    <td>Routing → Architect Flow Editor</td>
    <td class="sev-high">HIGH</td>
    <td>Shows toast: <i>"Draft saved"</i>. No actual persistence — flow edits are lost on navigation. Should write to <code>window.DB.flows</code>.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">AppFoundry Marketplace button</td>
    <td>Apps view</td>
    <td class="sev-medium">MEDIUM</td>
    <td>Toast pointing to external Genesys URL. Expected: an in-app catalogue or a working <code>target="_blank"</code> external link.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">"New chat" button (Directory)</td>
    <td>Directory workspace header</td>
    <td class="sev-medium">MEDIUM</td>
    <td>Shows a toast. Should navigate to the Activity view and open a new web-chat session.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Pagination controls (‹ › and "Rows per page ▾")</td>
    <td>All admin tables (footer)</td>
    <td class="sev-medium">MEDIUM</td>
    <td>Shows toast: <i>"All rows shown on one page"</i>. Controls should be visually greyed-out/disabled so users aren't confused.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>2C — Incomplete / Prototype-Only Features</h3>

<table class="issues">
  <tr>
    <th style="width:26%">Feature</th>
    <th style="width:18%">Location</th>
    <th style="width:12%">Severity</th>
    <th>Gap Description</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Calibrations CRUD</td>
    <td>Quality &amp; WEM → Calibrations</td>
    <td class="sev-high">HIGH</td>
    <td>Page renders static HTML only. Drawer opens a prototype form but nothing is saved. Unlike Evaluation Forms which has a full CRUD engine, Calibrations has no functional engine. Add/Edit/Delete are all non-functional.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Global search — Enter key</td>
    <td>Top bar search (#gs)</td>
    <td class="sev-medium">MEDIUM</td>
    <td>Dropdown with live suggestions works correctly, but pressing Enter does nothing. Should navigate to the first result.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Architect flow persistence</td>
    <td>Routing → Architect Flow Editor</td>
    <td class="sev-high">HIGH</td>
    <td>Flow changes live in memory only. Navigating away and returning reloads the original flow. Writes should be committed to <code>window.DB.flows[]</code>.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">No data persistence across page refresh</td>
    <td>Entire application</td>
    <td class="sev-critical">CRITICAL</td>
    <td>All data lives in <code>window.DB</code>. A browser refresh resets the entire platform. The <code>mcmExport()</code>/<code>mcmImport()</code> workaround exists but is buried and undiscoverable.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 3: UX DEAD-ENDS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>3. UX Dead-Ends &amp; Navigation Gaps</h2>

<p>These are interaction patterns where users get stuck, lose context, or reach a dead-end with no clear way forward.</p>

<ol class="recs">
  <li>
    <b>Browser Back/Forward buttons don't work for sub-views.</b><br>
    All sub-navigation (openPage, go) is DOM-only and does not update the browser URL. Clicking the browser's Back button navigates away from the app entirely instead of going to the previous admin page.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Use <code>history.pushState()</code> on each <code>openPage()</code> / <code>go()</code> call to keep the URL in sync.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Sidebar active indicator loses sync on breadcrumb navigation.</b><br>
    Clicking a breadcrumb link re-renders content but doesn't update the <code>.on</code> class on the sidebar link. The highlighted item stays on the last-clicked page.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Call <code>navMark(id)</code> whenever content is loaded via breadcrumb or any non-sidebar path.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>No deep-linkable URLs for any admin page.</b><br>
    Sharing a URL to "People" or "Queues" is impossible — all traffic lands on the same login screen. Useful for training (sharing links to specific pages with learners).<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Hash-based routing (<code>/#/admin/people</code>) enables deep links with zero backend changes.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Favourites tab is hardcoded, not personalised.</b><br>
    The Admin index "Favourites" tab is hardcoded to <code>['people','queues','flows','campaigns']</code>. Users cannot add or remove their own favourites.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Store favourites in <code>localStorage</code> and add a ★ toggle icon to each admin card.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>No empty-state messages in tables.</b><br>
    Filtering a table to zero results leaves a completely blank table body — no "No results found" message. This looks like a loading failure to users.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: In <code>filterRows()</code>, if <code>visibleRows === 0</code>, append a styled empty-state row.</span>
  </li>
</ol>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 4: UX IMPROVEMENTS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<h2>4. UX Improvement Suggestions</h2>

<h3>4A — Button Design &amp; Visual Hierarchy</h3>

<ol class="recs">
  <li>
    <b>Primary vs secondary button distinction is too weak.</b><br>
    The orange <code>.btn</code> (primary) and white <code>.btn.sec</code> (secondary) appear at the same height and font size. In dense page headers they can be confused.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Increase secondary button border weight to 1.5px, reduce its font weight to 500, add a subtle left margin between paired buttons.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Broken/placeholder buttons look identical to working ones.</b><br>
    Buttons like "Export", "Preview", and "Debug" are styled identically to fully functional buttons. Users click, see nothing or a toast, and lose trust.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Apply <code>opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed;</code> to all placeholder buttons, or wire them to real actions.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Destructive actions have no confirmation step.</b><br>
    Deleting a user, queue, flow, or trunk happens immediately on a single click. No "Are you sure?" step.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Change the delete button text to "Confirm delete?" for 2s before executing, or show a compact confirm dialog.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Top-bar icon buttons have no tooltips or labels.</b><br>
    The 🔔 (notifications), ⊙ (what's new), and ? (help) icons are raw character glyphs with no accessible label.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add <code>title="Notifications"</code>, <code>title="What's New"</code>, and <code>title="Help"</code> attributes plus aria-label for accessibility.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Row action "⋮" menu hit area is too small.</b><br>
    The three-dot overflow menu column is only 40px wide. Clicking it precisely on a dense table is frustrating.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Expand hit area to 48px minimum. Show hover-action row on the entire table row.</span>
  </li>
</ol>

<h3>4B — Navigation &amp; Wayfinding</h3>

<ol class="recs">
  <li>
    <b>No keyboard shortcut to focus global search.</b><br>
    Enterprise tools (Linear, Notion, Salesforce) all use Ctrl+K / ⌘+K. Users who know this pattern hit it instinctively and get no response.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add a 3-line keydown event listener: if Ctrl+K or ⌘+K, call <code>document.getElementById('gs').focus()</code>.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>No collapsible admin sidebar.</b><br>
    The left nav is always 246px wide. On a 1280px screen this leaves only ~1034px for content.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add a collapse toggle button at the top of #anav. When collapsed, show only group abbreviations with tooltips.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Global search Enter key does nothing.</b><br>
    The dropdown with live results is functional and excellent. But pressing Enter doesn't navigate — the user must click with the mouse.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add keyboard navigation (↑↓ to highlight, Enter to navigate) to the search dropdown results list.</span>
  </li>
</ol>

<h3>4C — Forms &amp; Drawers</h3>

<ol class="recs">
  <li>
    <b>No required-field indicators.</b><br>
    Fields that are mandatory (queue name, person email, trunk URI) don't show an asterisk or red border until after a failed save.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add * to required field labels. On validation failure, add a red border + inline error message below the field rather than only a toast.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Long dropdowns have no search filter.</b><br>
    Dropdowns like "Assign role", "Select queue", and "Choose flow" list all items as a plain &lt;select&gt;. With 50+ items scrolling to find a name is painful.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Replace long &lt;select&gt; elements with a searchable combobox pattern: an input + filterable &lt;ul&gt; positioned absolutely.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Drawer Save / Cancel buttons are not in a sticky footer.</b><br>
    On long drawers (e.g. Queue editor with 5 tabs, People editor with roles/skills) the Save and Cancel buttons scroll out of view.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Give drawer footers <code>position: sticky; bottom: 0;</code> with a white/shadow backdrop so action buttons are always visible.</span>
  </li>
</ol>

<h3>4D — Feedback, Data &amp; States</h3>

<ol class="recs">
  <li>
    <b>No persistent notification history.</b><br>
    Toast notifications auto-dismiss. Users who miss a toast have no way to review it. The bell shows only audit entries, not system toasts.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add a "Recent notifications" section to the bell dropdown showing the last 10 toasts with type + message + time.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>No loading / transition state.</b><br>
    Switching between heavy pages (Performance dashboard, Architect editor) has no loading indicator. On low-end hardware it can feel like the UI has frozen.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add a 150ms CSS fade-in on #cnt content swap and a thin orange progress bar at the top of the page during transitions.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Data persistence is undiscoverable.</b><br>
    The <code>mcmExport()</code> / <code>mcmImport()</code> functions let users save and restore their full DB state as JSON — but they're only accessible via the People page "Data" menu. New users will never find it.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add a "Save state / Restore" option to the profile/avatar dropdown alongside Sign Out.</span>
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Column filter chips don't work reliably on all pages.</b><br>
    "Division: All ▾" and "Status: Any ▾" chips operate on pre-rendered static DOM. On static SNAP pages they filter raw HTML text which is unreliable and can produce false matches.<br>
    <span style="color:#1a7a4a;font-size:10pt;">&#10003; Fix: Add a <code>data-filter-col</code> attribute to each page's table so the generic <code>chipFilter()</code> handler can identify the correct column index.</span>
  </li>
</ol>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 5: QUICK WINS
     ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>5. Quick Wins</h2>

<div class="callout callout-info">
  <b>&#128161; What counts as a Quick Win</b>
  These fixes require adding or changing a single attribute, a few lines of CSS, or wiring an existing function. No new engines or architectural changes needed. Estimated effort per item: 5–30 minutes.
</div>

<table class="qw">
  <tr>
    <th style="width:5%">#</th>
    <th style="width:30%">Fix</th>
    <th style="width:32%">Code Change Required</th>
    <th>User Impact</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-weight:bold;color:#b3261e;">1</td>
    <td><b>Wire "Audit Viewer" button</b></td>
    <td><code>onclick="auditDrawer()"</code></td>
    <td>Enables the audit log drawer from Admin home — currently unreachable from this button.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-weight:bold;color:#b3261e;">2</td>
    <td><b>Wire "What's New" button</b></td>
    <td><code>onclick="dd('wnddm')"</code></td>
    <td>Shows the existing changelog dropdown. Zero new code required.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-weight:bold;color:#c9401a;">3</td>
    <td><b>Wire ⊙ and ? top-bar icons</b></td>
    <td><code>onclick="dd('wnddm')"</code> and <code>onclick="dd('helpddm')"</code></td>
    <td>Both dropdowns already exist. Wiring takes ~5 seconds per icon.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-weight:bold;color:#c9401a;">4</td>
    <td><b>Add tooltips to all top-bar icons</b></td>
    <td>Add <code>title="Notifications"</code> etc. to each .ic div</td>
    <td>Immediate discoverability and accessibility improvement.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-weight:bold;color:#c9401a;">5</td>
    <td><b>Visually disable pagination controls</b></td>
    <td>CSS: <code>.pgr span { opacity:.4; cursor:not-allowed; }</code></td>
    <td>Removes the misleading click-and-nothing experience without any JS changes.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-weight:bold;color:#c9401a;">6</td>
    <td><b>Expose Export/Save state in avatar menu</b></td>
    <td>Add a menu item calling <code>mcmExport()</code> to <code>#meddm</code> dropdown</td>
    <td>Makes the only data-save mechanism discoverable before users lose work to a refresh.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-weight:bold;color:#8a5c00;">7</td>
    <td><b>Ctrl+K / ⌘+K to focus search</b></td>
    <td>3-line JS keydown event listener on document</td>
    <td>Power-user UX that aligns with common enterprise keyboard shortcuts.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="font-weight:bold;color:#8a5c00;">8</td>
    <td><b>Empty-state row in all tables</b></td>
    <td>In <code>filterRows()</code>: if visibleRows === 0, append a "No results" row</td>
    <td>Eliminates the blank-table confusion across all 60+ admin pages simultaneously.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

