<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 7: ARCHITECTURE NOTE
     ═══════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h2>7. Architecture Note — Unused Component Library</h2>

<div class="callout callout-info">
  <b>&#128230; Unused React Component Library</b>
  The project has a full <b>shadcn/ui + Radix UI + Tailwind CSS</b> component library installed (accordion, dialog, drawer, select, combobox, tooltip, and 40+ others). None of these components are currently used — the entire UI is vanilla JS injected via <code>dangerouslySetInnerHTML</code>.
</div>

<p>These components could replace custom CSS patterns for drawers, dropdowns, tooltips, and confirmation dialogs. Radix primitives include ARIA roles and keyboard navigation out of the box, providing accessibility for free.</p>

<table class="issues">
  <tr>
    <th style="width:22%">Component</th>
    <th style="width:22%">Already installed?</th>
    <th>How it helps</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Tooltip (Radix)</td>
    <td style="color:#1a7a4a;font-weight:bold;">Yes — installed</td>
    <td>Replace character-glyph icon buttons with Tooltip wrappers for instant accessible hover labels. Covers all top-bar icons and the "⋮" row menus.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">AlertDialog (Radix)</td>
    <td style="color:#1a7a4a;font-weight:bold;">Yes — installed</td>
    <td>Drop-in accessible confirmation dialog for all destructive actions. Blocks until the user confirms, preventing accidental deletes.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Command (cmdk)</td>
    <td style="color:#1a7a4a;font-weight:bold;">Yes — installed</td>
    <td><code>cmdk</code> is already a dependency. Replacing the custom #gs global search with a &lt;Command&gt; palette would give Ctrl+K, keyboard navigation, fuzzy search, and result grouping for free.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Sonner (toast)</td>
    <td style="color:#1a7a4a;font-weight:bold;">Yes — installed</td>
    <td>Replacing the custom toast system with Sonner adds toast types (success/error/warning/info), a notification queue, and programmatic dismissal.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td class="name">Select / Combobox</td>
    <td style="color:#1a7a4a;font-weight:bold;">Yes — installed</td>
    <td>Radix Select with a search input inside would replace all long plain &lt;select&gt; dropdowns (user picker, queue picker, flow picker) with a searchable, keyboard-navigable component.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

